ForceSmart's two-phase anchor controller is adapted from:

- xiaobright/dsh-anchored-standard at
  d97bec91a3d668f4cf1d03ee5f20aae84fb6f85c (MIT)
- zhu1090093659/dsh-web-ui packages/dsh-liangshen at
  3647a33fa467e0335260468614f6eed04b196c38 (Apache-2.0 package;
  its tool-bootstrap.mjs is attributed to dsh-anchored-standard under MIT)

The dsh-TUI adaptation keeps base preset, plan/goal policy, fork lineage, and
restricted child-agent behavior separate from the original standalone preset.
Its clean first request uses the official Minimal persona plus model-facing
Bash/editor prompts and schemas. Execution reuses compatible base-preset tools
where possible and may mount the official DSH implementations only for a
top-level agent; child scopes never gain tools. The pinned Anchored main has no
default output cap, while ForceSmart deliberately keeps the fixed reference
composition's 1024 bootstrap budget and trajectory gate.
These implementation sources are attribution and design references only; the
product, command, and UI name is ForceSmart.
